            <ArticleTitle>[Changes in cerebral circulation under the influence of korinfar in hypertension patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of the characteristic changes of the cerebral blood circulation in patients with hypertensive disease after corinfar intakes indicates that the cerebral blood flow and self-feeling of the patients varied depending on the initial state of the cerebral blood flow. &quot;Hypotonic&quot; disorders of the cerebral blood flow are less favourable for corinfar treatment as compared with the &quot;spastic&quot; disturbances.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
